# Keep build contexts small, but not so aggressive that COPY silently copies
# nothing. The previous version excluded DATA/ and MODELS/ wholesale, which
# would have made `COPY MODELS/ ./MODELS/` fail at build time.
#
# Exclusions are therefore per-file rather than per-directory, so it is obvious
# what does and does not reach an image.

.git/
.gitattributes
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Analysis lives outside the runtime images.
NOTEBOOKS/
REPORTS/
infra/
mlruns/
*.md
!README.md

# Local config never goes into an image - compose and ECS supply the real values.
.env

# --- data ------------------------------------------------------------------ #
# DATA/raw holds the committed SQLite database (3 MB). Every image needs it:
# the model job trains from it, and both the API and the dashboard rebuild the
# feature panel from it at startup.
DATA/MIG_Cement_Records.db          # duplicate of DATA/raw - not the configured path
DATA/interim/
DATA/processed/operations_feature_engineered.parquet

# per_site_sigma.parquet and test_forecasts.parquet are small and wanted:
# sigma drives per-site safety stock, and without it the API silently falls back
# to a single estate-wide figure.

# --- models ---------------------------------------------------------------- #
# The API image bakes the artefact so it deploys to ECS as one unit. Only the
# two files that matter, not the whole directory.
MODELS/*
!MODELS/rf_demand_forecaster.joblib
!MODELS/rf_demand_forecaster_meta.json
